    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0122" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg82"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward. to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1227.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 10, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Great destruction of rebel communications
                    has been accomplished by General Grierson in Mississippi, and the insurgents
                    have suffered severe loss by the burning of their storehouses at Charlotte,
                    North Carolina. With these exceptions, no important military movements have been
                    made during the past week. Congress resumed its labors on the 6th instant. The
                    debates are temperate, as the measures discussed are grave.</p>
                <p>It is a circumstance of much significance that the legislature of Kentucky is
                    earnestly debating the subject of slavery. The parties divided between the
                    policy of immediate abolition and that of gradual emancipation.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(Same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis,</hi> to all oar principal
                        ministers in Europe.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
